{"Tests use time.sleep to allow background processing which is fragile - consider using synchronization primitives (Event) or polling a condition with short timeout to make tests less timing-dependent": 0.6164249777793884, "Unrelated/accidental doc change included (CLAUDE.md) - small unrelated examples about hasattr vs isinstance should be removed from the PR": 0.6329138875007629, "Default for flusher processes CLI option is set to 1, which reduces parallelism relative to previous behavior where it was one process per shard - consider making CLI default None or 0 to map to 'auto' behavior": 0.7175634503364563, "process_restarts counter is never reset - many small flaps spaced out in time could accumulate restarts and eventually force a consumer restart even if flaps are infrequent. Consider implementing decay restarts over time or reset count when process has been healthy for X seconds": 0.3208589255809784, "multiprocessing.Value objects used for process_healthy_since and process_backpressure_since have different semantics when accessed from threading.Threads (in tests) vs multiprocessing.Process (in production) - be mindful of different concurrency model behaviors": 0.19089668989181519, "Health metrics tagging could be enhanced by adding process index tag to make it easier to map metrics to processes in dashboards": 0.09407123923301697}